{
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-append-growth",
      "text": "The capacity append chooses when it grows is not modelled: a grown append's backing is fresh and its capacity is [\"unknown\", \"growth\"]."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-errors-nonnil",
      "text": "errors.New and fmt.Errorf return non-nil errors, and so does a package variable of an error type that the package initializer assigns from one of them."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-nil-deref-not-modelled",
      "text": "Nil pointer dereferences are not partiality sites."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-opaque-calls",
      "text": "Calls outside the analyzed packages that are not primitives are opaque: their results are call terms, and what they do to memory they can reach is unknown."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-prim:(github.com/morph-l2/go-ethereum/common.Hash).Bytes",
      "text": "Hash.Bytes() has a value receiver and returns h[:], a 32-byte slice over the receiver's copy: a fresh backing array whose element k is h[k]."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-prim:github.com/morph-l2/go-ethereum/common.BytesToHash",
      "text": "BytesToHash(b) is the 32-byte array holding b right-aligned (common/types.go: SetBytes crops b to its last 32 bytes, then copies it to h[32-len(b):]); for len(b) == 32 element k is b[k]."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json",
      "id": "go-prim:github.com/morph-l2/go-ethereum/crypto.Keccak256Hash",
      "text": "Keccak256Hash(data...) is the keccak-256 digest of the concatenated arguments: an opaque HASH sink; it reads its arguments and retains none of them."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_header.extracted.json",
      "id": "A-dirty",
      "text": "Memory at the free pointer is not zeroed: every region a walk allocates (mload(0x40)) starts with unknown cells (memory_init dirty), so a byte that no op writes is unknown, never zero."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_header.extracted.json",
      "id": "A-env",
      "text": "Environment terms (storage, block, msg and tx members, blobhash, results of external calls, memory reads, and values computed from them) are free: a revert whose failing condition mentions one belongs to the transition, not to the edge (rule J1), and conditions on them are projected away."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_header.extracted.json",
      "id": "A-implicit",
      "text": "Implicit reverts (checked arithmetic, array bounds, ABI decoding) are not part of an edge's partiality: only explicit require, revert and branch conditions on inputs are."
    },
    {
      "document": "spec/M2/facts/morph_header.extracted.json",
      "fields": [
        "batchIndex",
        "totalL1MessagePopped"
      ],
      "id": "A-width:Header",
      "record": "Header",
      "text": "Fields of Header whose value type is wider than their stored width: the bytes keep only the low part of the value, so they determine it only when it fits the width."
    },
    {
